\f1\fs22 \'93Patch?\'94 asked a pretty young blonde in scrubs, pigtails bobbing, as Sarah woke up.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 \'93How\'92d you\'97?\'94 Sarah glanced at the door, calculating escape.\
\'93Nancy called,\'94 the intruder said, settling beside her on the bed with a transparent envelope containing a bandage patch half the size of Sarah\'92s palm. \'93She says you\'92re unwell?\'94\
Sarah flinched.\
\'93For your nausea,\'94 the intruder explained.\
\'93It seems every doctor in the Ghetto moonlights as a drug dealer,\'94 Sarah croaked.\
\'93I\'92m not from the Ghetto,\'94 the woman replied, sidestepping the second accusation with decorous grace. \'93Seriously, it\'92s just for the nausea. You\'92ll be right as Airborne rain in no time, pretty woman.\'94 She kissed Sarah\'92s cheek\'97something Sarah found reassuring once the shock subsided\'97then knelt and applied the patch to Sarah\'92s arm with surgical flair.\
Sarah noted the matching patch on the woman\'92s own arm. \'93Is that what yours is for?\'94\
The woman laughed and fluttered her lashes. \'93Do I look like someone who\'92s ever nauseous?\'94\
\'93No. Though neither am I. Not usually.\'94\
\'93Well, I suppose the odd blimp in health must squiggle across all our charts.\'94\
\'93Blip. You mean blip.\'94\
\'93Do I?\'94 The woman smiled. \'93Anyway, we\'92ll see when the results come in.\'94\
Sarah\'92s heart skipped. \'93Results?\'94\
\'93Sent your samples to the lab ten minutes ago. Blood, DNA, urine\'97with no small amount of skill and experience, I assure you.\'94 She blushed, made her smile humbler. \'93I\'92m Dr Logan. Katherine\'97Kathy.\'94 She gave Sarah a vigorous hug. \'93News in about forty minutes. Now I need sleep.\'94\
Kathy curled away, faced the wall, and fell so still Sarah suspected a coma.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Sarah woke to the bleating of a lamb\'97Kathy\'92s tablet alarm. The doctor sat up, retrieved another patch from her medical bag, ripped off the old one and applied the fresh one with casual expertise.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 \'93I\'92ve got about forty minutes of lucidity,\'94 she announced, rebooted. \'93Let\'92s look at the results.\'94\
Sarah huddled under the blankets and watched as Kathy tapped and scrolled on her breakfast-tray-sized screen.\
\'93Slightly elevated temperature... clean DNA... no viruses or bacteria... toxicology clear. Aw, no recreationals?\'94 Kathy grinned. Sarah stared back, wide-eyed and blank, like a guilty child.\
\'93Hmm.\'94 Kathy stiffened. \'93Quite extraordinary. You\'92re\'97\'94 She lapsed into medical word salad only an oncologist-virologist-gynaecologist-astrologer-vacuum-salesman could manage.\
\'93Stop,\'94 Sarah rasped.\
Kathy regarded Sarah pulling blankets to her chin. She licked and pursed her lips.\
\'93None of this is a surprise to you, is it?\'94 Kathy made it a statement.\
Sarah gulped, wishing she could swallow the entire conversation.\
\'93Who are you?\'94 Kathy whispered.\
Sarah shook like a frightened doe. \'93I\'92m just... I\'92m just\'85\'94\
\'93Invincible,\'94 Kathy said, barely above a whisper.\
Sarah trembled.\
Kathy recovered her bedside manner, despite being on the bed rather than beside it. \'93Well, this certainly makes your other condition a little easier.\'94\
\'93Other condition?\'94\
\'93You know: your pregnancy.\'94\
\'93Pregnancy?\'94 Sarah repeated.\
Kathy ground her eyebrows together. \'93You didn\'92t know?\'94\
\'93I was told I could never fall pregnant.\'94 Sarah felt the skein of her life untangle.\
Kathy clamped her jaw.\
Sarah\'92s mind conjured the night of the Vegas Show, and where she\'92d spent the night after, and with whom.\
\'93Damn you, Tony, you taxing rapist!\'94
